diff --git a/docs/v0.20.1-release-notes.md b/docs/v0.20.1-release-notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c09ce3108e2946ff0c2db0e8685c5ee9ba3f24f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/v0.20.1-release-notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Project Constellation 0.20.1 — All-Tab Chat Guardian Hotfix
+
+Project Constellation 0.20.1 builds directly on the immutable 0.20.0 Reliability Foundation and hardens ChatGPT continuity against the current site’s newer stream-recovery/error surfaces. The goal is simple: unfinished work should keep moving across every open ChatGPT tab without losing state, replaying unsafe side effects, or requiring the user to babysit error banners.
+
+## All-tab Chat Guardian
+
+- **Every open ChatGPT conversation is supervised independently.** The background guardian enumerates the full open-tab set and fans health/recovery checks out with `Promise.allSettled`, so one unresponsive or broken tab cannot hold the others hostage.
+- **Background tabs stay eligible for recovery.** Recoverable ChatGPT tabs are marked non-auto-discardable when Chrome permits it; already-discarded tabs are reloaded without foreground focus. Chrome 132+ frozen tabs are detected explicitly, skipped instead of accumulating queued probes, and reconciled immediately on unfreeze/activation.
+- **Event-first recovery.** Explicit failure/stall state changes schedule an immediate guardian sweep. An adaptive one-shot alarm is retained only as a bounded safety fallback; there is no permanent fixed guardian polling loop.
+- **Bounded state and deduplication.** Per-chat failure fingerprints, continuation attempts, reload attempts, cooldowns, and recent recovery history are persisted so the same error cannot trigger an uncontrolled retry/reload loop.
+
+## New ChatGPT error handling
+
+0.20.1 recognizes the current ChatGPT stream-recovery failure family, including the observed message:
+
+`ChatGPT stream recovery polling timed out`
+
+It also recognizes semantically equivalent current-turn stream/response timeout and failure wording so a minor text change does not break recovery. If ChatGPT changes the sentence more substantially but still exposes a native current-turn **Retry / Try again** affordance beside failure-like copy, Constellation treats that recovery-control-anchored surface as an interruption without depending on one exact string. Detection remains scoped to the current frontier and guarded against ordinary assistant prose that merely discusses timeouts or recovery architecture.
+
+## Safe continuation instead of Retry replay
+
+When the guardian proves that the current task is unfinished and the tab is in a recoverable failure/stall state, it sends one simple new user turn:
+
+`Continue the unfinished task.`
+
+That is deliberately separate from ChatGPT’s native **Retry / Try again / Regenerate** control. Constellation does not automatically click that native control because replaying a failed turn can duplicate external tool calls, writes, uploads, or other side effects whose completion may be uncertain.
+
+The continuation sender:
+
+- validates the expected chat before acting;
+- requires an unresolved/current user task;
+- refuses to wake a healthy completed chat;
+- refuses to overwrite a non-empty composer or user draft;
+- stages text through current ChatGPT composer variants and waits for a usable Send control;
+- fingerprints the continuation in page/session state where available so the same recovery is not emitted repeatedly.
+
+## Holds that remain protected
+
+Automatic continuation never bypasses provider-review/security gates, connected-app/tool approvals, sign-in/authentication requirements, rate limits/cooldowns, unavailable/deleted conversations, or conversation-capacity handoff states. These remain explicit holds rather than being reclassified as recoverable errors.
+
+## Bounded reload fallback
+
+A reload is allowed only for an explicit terminal failure when the separate continuation cannot be staged or sent because the current composer/send surface is unavailable. It is capped to one reload per failure fingerprint. A busy composer/user draft is never cleared or reloaded over.
+
+## Regression coverage
+
+0.20.1 adds dedicated coverage for:
+
+- exact, future-form, and recovery-control-anchored stream/error classification;
+- semantic false-positive rejection;
+- every-open-tab fanout, frozen/discarded-tab reconciliation, and per-tab failure isolation;
+- healthy/completed tabs remaining untouched;
+- user-draft and protected-hold preservation;
+- native Retry controls never being auto-clicked;
+- one-shot guardian fallback scheduling rather than fixed polling;
+- bounded reload fallback and failure-fingerprint deduplication;
+- real Chromium DOM recovery of multiple independent failed ChatGPT-like tabs;
+- background integration proving only failed tabs receive `Continue the unfinished task.`.
+
+## Release lineage
+
+0.20.0 remains immutable. 0.20.1 is a source-compatible hotfix lineage built from the exact verified 0.20.0 source archive plus the 0.20.1 delta. All 0.20.0 provider/permission coverage, stable extension identity, desktop compatibility identifiers, Update Center behavior, and existing reliability/security contracts remain required release gates.
